1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,304
Claude can now join your Google Meet call and start building the plan while you talk.

2
00:00:04,354 --> 00:00:06,693
It's called Claude Meetings.

3
00:00:06,743 --> 00:00:10,540
Say, Claude, start a doc, and teammates edit it live.

4
00:00:10,590 --> 00:00:14,010
Ask for a timeline, and it draws one on a whiteboard.

5
00:00:14,060 --> 00:00:15,096
The best part?

6
00:00:15,146 --> 00:00:19,540
During the beta, notes and transcripts are free on Team and Enterprise plans.

7
00:00:19,590 --> 00:00:23,205
Docs and whiteboards are free until February twenty twenty-seven.

8
00:00:23,255 --> 00:00:25,395
A coffee pot, Muja?

9
00:00:25,445 --> 00:00:31,785
Fun fact: the first webcam, as it's often called, watched a coffee pot at Cambridge in 1991.

10
00:00:31,835 --> 00:00:32,757
Alright...

11
00:00:32,807 --> 00:00:34,225
back to our story.

12
00:00:34,275 --> 00:00:35,360
Now the catch.

13
00:00:35,410 --> 00:00:38,407
It's Google Meet only, on Team and Enterprise plans.

14
00:00:38,457 --> 00:00:41,540
Zoom, Teams and personal plans must wait.

15
00:00:41,590 --> 00:00:43,120
Privacy matters too.

16
00:00:43,170 --> 00:00:48,214
It keeps a transcript, not the audio, and posts a notice in the chat when it joins.

17
00:00:48,264 --> 00:00:49,833
Is it a secret agent?

18
00:00:49,883 --> 00:00:51,237
No, Muja.

19
00:00:51,287 --> 00:00:53,643
Still, ask everyone first.

20
00:00:53,693 --> 00:00:54,971
So what should you do?

21
00:00:55,021 --> 00:00:56,476
Tell your team first.

22
00:00:56,526 --> 00:00:58,247
Skip client calls.

23
00:00:58,297 --> 00:01:00,071
Pilot one weekly meeting.

24
00:01:00,121 --> 00:01:04,968
My take: a faster first draft, not someone who will own the actions.

25
00:01:05,018 --> 00:01:08,662
Handy for internal Google Meet calls, wait-and-see for the rest.

26
00:01:08,712 --> 00:01:11,103
The full review is on my blog.
